10
00:50:00,000 --> 00:50:06,000
Granny, played by Adrian Ricard.

11
00:55:00,000 --> 00:55:06,000
I, Robot (sometimes stylized as i,Robot) is a 2004 American science fiction action film
directed by Alex Proyas, from a screenplay by Jeff Vintar and Akiva Goldsman.

12
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
It stars Will Smith, Bridget Moynahan, Bruce
Greenwood, James Cromwell, and Alan Tudyk.

13
01:05:00,000 --> 01:05:06,000
The film is named after  Isaac Asimov's 1950 short-story collection and incorporates Asimov's
three laws of robotics and several characters, though it is not a direct adaptation.

14
01:10:00,000 --> 01:10:06,000
The film is set in Chicago in 2035.

15
01:15:00,000 --> 01:15:06,000
Highly intelligent robots fill public service positions throughout the world,
operating under the Three Laws of Robotics to keep humans safe.

16
01:20:00,000 --> 01:20:06,000
Detective Del Spooner (Smith) investigates the alleged suicide of U.S.

17
01:25:00,000 --> 01:25:06,000
Robotics founder Alfred Lanning (Cromwell) and believes that a
human-like robot called Sonny (Tudyk) murdered him.

18
01:30:00,000 --> 01:30:06,000
I, Robot was released in the United States on July 16, 2004.

19
01:35:00,000 --> 01:35:06,000
Produced with a budget of $105–120 million, the film grossed $353.1 million worldwide and received mixed
reviews from critics, with praise for the visual effects and acting, but criticism of the plot.

20
01:40:00,000 --> 01:40:06,000
At the 77th Academy Awards, the film was nominated for Best Visual Effects.

21
01:45:00,000 --> 01:45:06,000
The film explores themes of chicago, illinois, future, man vs
machine, hero, artificial intelligence (a.i.).

22
01:50:00,000 --> 01:50:06,000
The tone is thought_provoking and intense.
